e,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-01-06T11:24:41Z","updated_at":"2025-11-22T08:51:07Z","closed_at":"2025-11-21T10:32:07Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101177","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101177","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101177.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101177.patch","merged_at":"2025-11-21T10:32:07Z"},"body":"Same rationale as #101105 and #101040, this time for `1.1-stable`. The commits are cherry-picked from #101105, minus the mingw one which wasn't needed.\r\n\r\nFor that release we still have original binaries, albeit the Linux ones are not properly portable, as they are compiled against openssl as a shared library, and the old 1.0.x version of openssl it used is hardly provided in Linux distros anymore (and if it is, it's with packager-defined SONAME which make it incompatible anyway, at least between Debian/RedHat families of distros).\r\n\r\nSo reusing the same setup as for `1.0-stable`, I'm going to remake Linux binaries, suffixed `_portable`.\r\n\r\nHere they are: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-builds/releases/tag/1.1-stable\r\n\r\nThe new `_portable` binaries have been compiled with the same Linux SDK we use for current 4.x releases, using GCC 13.2.0 compiled against glibc 2.28, so it should be supported on most Linux distros newer than Ubuntu 18.04 (excluded).\r\n\r\nI also updated the export templates tpz with a new `_portable.tpz`, where the Linux export templates have been replaced by the new builds.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"ht